// Standing regression fixture for ARC Task 6 review, rounds 2 and 3.
//
// Round 2 (reviewer Critical): a global's OWN Init expression never routed
// through lowCountedStore's retain-on-store -- cpEmitGlobalsInit's
// Init-emission path plain-assigned a bare-alias Init's handle with NO
// retain (`cv_g2 = cv_g1;`), so Task 6's new unconditional cl_free_globals
// double-released an rc==1 handle: reviewer-reproduced `rt_rc:
// over-release`, exit 134, under CLARUS_MEM_STRICT+CLARUS_MEM_PARANOID.
// Fixed by giving the Init path its own birth-vs-retain classification
// (irGlobalInitBirth, set by lowGlobalVarDecl using the SAME
// lowStoreIsBirth/lowStoreIntrOwnsResult rule a runtime store uses) and
// retaining a non-birth Init's value right after the plain-assign --
// cpEmitGlobalsInit's own comment (cprint.cla) has the full account.
//
// gaT1/gaT2 pin the reviewer's exact TEXT repro (`var g2: text = g1`).
// gaL1/gaL2 pin the LIST-OF-TEXT variant -- the retain lands on the LIST
// CONTAINER's own handle (cpEmitRetain's KList branch), not its elements.
//
// Round 3 (reviewer Critical, found during round 2's own verification and
// escalated back into this task rather than deferred): cpEmitRelease's
// element-release walk (list/map deep release) ran UNCONDITIONALLY on
// every release call-site, before the container's own release -- so once
// gaL1/gaL2 shared one list handle (round 2's fix), a list WITH an element
// present at exit crashed anyway: the first release site walked and freed
// the element, the second site walked the SAME (already-freed) element
// again. Fixed by gating the element walk on rt_list_lastref/
// rt_map_lastref (runtime/host/rt_core.inc) -- a NULL-safe "is this
// the box's only live reference" (rc==1) check read BEFORE either site's
// own release call decrements it. gaL1/gaL2 below now push an element and
// leave it in place at exit (round 2's version popped it back out first,
// working around round 3's bug without saying so out loud in the code --
// no longer necessary). gaM1/gaM2 pin the MAP-OF-TEXT variant of the same
// shape. gaL3/local2 (inside the func body) pin a local aliasing a global
// container WITH an element present.
//
// ARC Task 8 update: this comment previously claimed `local2`'s own
// scope-exit release stayed SHALLOW (Task 4's per-function escape pass,
// `lowFreeUnsafe`, used to disqualify an aliased local from a deep
// release) -- that apparatus is deleted now, so `local2` gets a full,
// unconditional DEEP release like every other scope-exit candidate (ARC
// Task 8). This is STILL safe, for a different reason than the one this
// comment used to give: `local2` and `gaL3` share one list handle at
// rc==2; `local2` releases first (function scope exit, `rt_list_lastref`
// reads rc==2 -> false, element walk skipped, rc drops to 1);
// `cl_free_globals` releases `gaL3` later, at process exit (SAME handle,
// `rt_list_lastref` reads rc==1 -> true, element walk fires, releases
// "loc", rc drops to 0) -- exactly one element-walk, on the release that
// actually destroys the container (Task 6 round 3's own guard, confirmed
// by reading the emitted C, not just assumed). Kept as a fixture anyway:
// it pins this disposition permanently, not just as of this commit.
//
// Expected strict-mode leak count: 0 (see ../arc_global_alias.leaks --
// absent, defaults to want-0) for all three pairs plus the local case.
//
// ARC Task 8 additions (pinning two carry-forward bugs this task fixed,
// per the brief's own "fixture it" / "do not leave it unresolved"
// instructions -- both were only hand-probed during development before
// this commit):
//
//   - `gaM1.get("k", "x" + "y")` below hits `IMapGetDvBirth`'s
//     PRESENT-key path: the default (`"x" + "y"`, a fresh concat -- birth)
//     is NOT the value returned (the key already exists, from the
//     "map-alias-ok" block above), so the default's own box must be
//     released as an orphan (known open leak bug 2's exact present-key
//     case widen_text.cla's own `.get("missing", ...)` call, absent-key
//     only, never exercised).
//   - `gaLL` (global `list of list of text`) pins the nested-container
//     deep-release walk (known open leak bug 3): `innerList` (a LOCAL) is
//     pushed into `gaLL` (retained, non-birth) and also kept alive by its
//     own local scope-exit release, so the shared inner list's rc==2 at
//     `innerList`'s own release (skips the walk, `rt_list_lastref` false,
//     drops to rc==1) and rc==1 at `gaLL`'s OWN release, at process exit
//     (walks and frees both the inner list's own "nested" element and the
//     inner list itself, `rt_list_lastref` true) -- exactly the recursive
//     `cpEmitRelease` shape `cpEmitRelease`'s own doc comment describes.
//
// ARC Task 8 review round 2 (Important finding, post-approval): a bare
// `lst.pop();`/`lst.shift();` STATEMENT is legal Clarus (checker accepts
// it -- the result is simply an expression statement whose value is
// unused) and used to leak the popped element permanently: cprint's
// IListPop/IListShift printer materialized the result into an UNTRACKED
// temp (`fpNewTmp`) and unconditionally hands it off (never releases it),
// which is correct for the assign/return/call-argument positions (some
// OTHER slot claims ownership there) but wrong for a bare, discarded
// statement, where NOTHING claims it. `popList` below pins the fix:
// `.pop()` then `.shift()`, both discarded, both now released at the end
// of their own statement (`fpDiscardExprIdx`, cprint.cla -- see its own
// doc comment for exactly how the discarded position is detected without
// touching the assign/return/call-argument shapes at all). No map-flavored
// analog exists to pin alongside it: map has no ordered pop/shift
// (`lowMapMethod` only lowers get/has/remove/count -- `.remove(k)` is
// void, already releases the evicted value internally, never a
// discardable non-void result in the first place).

var gaT1: text = "hello"
var gaT2: text = gaT1

var gaL1: list of text
var gaL2: list of text = gaL1

var gaM1: map of text
var gaM2: map of text = gaM1

var gaL3: list of text

var gaLL: list of list of text

func runArcGlobalAlias() {
    var buf: char[64]
    var n: int
    var s: string
    var local2: list of text
    var innerList: list of text
    var popList: list of text

    n = gaT1.toBytes(buf)
    s.fromBytes(buf, n)
    alert(s)

    n = gaT2.toBytes(buf)
    s.fromBytes(buf, n)
    alert(s)

    gaL1.push("shared")
    if gaL2.count == 1 and gaL2.first() == "shared" {
        alert("list-alias-ok")
    } else {
        alert("list-alias-bad")
    }

    gaM1["k"] = "v"
    if gaM2.has("k") and gaM2["k"] == "v" {
        alert("map-alias-ok")
    } else {
        alert("map-alias-bad")
    }

    gaL3.push("loc")
    local2 = gaL3
    if local2.count == 1 and local2.first() == "loc" {
        alert("local-alias-ok")
    } else {
        alert("local-alias-bad")
    }

    // ARC Task 8, known open leak bug 2: key PRESENT, birth default --
    // the default must be released as an orphan, not leaked.
    if gaM1.get("k", "x" + "y") == "v" {
        alert("get-present-birth-ok")
    } else {
        alert("get-present-birth-bad")
    }

    // ARC Task 8, known open leak bug 3: nested container deep release.
    innerList.add("nested")
    gaLL.add(innerList)
    if gaLL.count == 1 and gaLL[0].count == 1 and gaLL[0][0] == "nested" {
        alert("nested-list-ok")
    } else {
        alert("nested-list-bad")
    }

    // ARC Task 8 review round 2: discarded pop()/shift() results leak.
    popList.add("x")
    popList.add("y")
    popList.add("z")
    popList.pop()
    popList.shift()
    if popList.count == 1 and popList.first() == "y" {
        alert("discard-pop-ok")
    } else {
        alert("discard-pop-bad")
    }
}
